273:    *           up.connect(down.<String>onSuccess(value -> {
274:    *             try {
275:    *               down.success(value.toUpperCase());
276:    *             } catch (Throwable e) {
277:    *               down.error(e);
278:    *             }
279:    *           }))
280:    *         )
281:    *     );
282:    *
283:    *     assertEquals("FOO", result.getValue());
284:    *   }
285:    * }
286:    * }</pre>
287:    * <p>
288:    * The “upstreamTransformer” function takes an upstream data source, and returns another upstream that wraps it.
289:    * It is typical for the returned upstream to invoke the {@link Upstream#connect(Downstream)} method of the given upstream during its connect method.
290:    * <p>
291:    * For more examples of transform implementations, please see the implementations of the methods of this interface.
292:    *
